"""clubs.py: parametric golf club heads for PinPoint Studio, built in Blender (bpy, headless).

Every head is our own geometry: a signed-distance model written in numpy, sampled on a voxel
grid, polygonised by OpenVDB (bundled with Blender), then given attribute-driven materials.
Hosel sleeve, ferrule, shaft stub and sleeve index marks are lathe / text meshes.

    Blender -b --factory-startup --python clubs.py -- --club driver [--h 0.2]

writes work/<club>.blend and work/<club>_meta.json (3-D anchor geometry for render.py).

World frame (mm), right-handed golfer at address, face square:
    +X toward the target, +Y toward the golfer (heel side), +Z up, ground z = 0.
"""
